 "description": "Plan section 10 layer 5's karne hook, the cheap seam the harness gave:\nthe sweep already holds both rendered frames' bytes per case, so each\ngrade-sweep and v2-sweep case now prints an IEEE CRC32 frameDigest\nline (cpu:.. gpu:..) beside the stats line - two builds that agree on\nmaxDiffLsb but disagree on content still disagree here (the stats\nbucket rounds 1-2 LSB jitter to the same line; the CRC does not).\nThe before/after-merge device comparison the plan names greps these\nlines; the pure function is pinned against the standard vectors\n(empty -> 0, 123456789 -> 0xCBF43926). The v1<->v2 run itself stays\nthe owner's device leg.\n\nFound-by-test: the first CRC draft kept Long's high bits (the\nstandard algorithm is 32-bit throughout) - the 123456789 vector\ncaught it.\n\nGates: gradle assembleDebug + testDebugUnitTest green (2877 tests, 0\nfailures). build-desktop.sh green (33 suites).",
